q=dict(question='When a later heartbeat context confirms a prefix containing distinct remote read requests, does response propagation preserve the origin and context of each returned status, as required by exact-context completion at the requester?',importance='Mis-correlation can discard a completed authority check for an earlier admitted remote read and cause avoidable timeout; no stale-read or whole-cluster liveness consequence is established.',source_ids=['S-read-queue','S-read-response','S-follower-read','S-client-batches','S-node-read','S-read-api'],participants=['Leader','Two remote read-origin nodes','Voting heartbeat responders'],objects=['readStatus','SystemCtx','ReadIndexResp','node-local read batch'],contexts=['Stable term and membership','Distinct pending read contexts','Latest context reaches quorum before an earlier context'],event_paths=['node.handleReadIndex -> Peer.ReadIndex -> follower forwarding -> leader queue -> heartbeat confirmation -> remote response -> follower readiness -> exact batch lookup'],activity_classes=['A2'],behavior_ids=['B-read-confirm','B-read-deliver'],fact_ids=['F-confirmed-read'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B-read-admit':'Registers actual request context and sends probes after current-term commit.','B-read-client':'Exact-key consumer establishes relevance of preserving each context.','B-authority':'Term and role admission constrain a legal schedule.','B-persistence':'Peer driver must honor state/message persistence ordering.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['Local-origin returned statuses use s.ctx correctly.','Duplicate context admission is coalesced, so distinct contexts are necessary.','Timeout remains a permitted client outcome; this question concerns response correlation, not a numeric success deadline.'],unknowns=['Find an applicable per-request correlation responsibility and determine whether a latest-context remote response has any alternative completion interpretation.','Construct a legal Peer-level history with current-term commit and overlapping remote reads, retaining actual heartbeat provenance.'],trigger_rationale='The producer returns each status with its own ctx, but remote emission substitutes m.Hint/m.HintHigh while follower and pendingReadIndex consume exact received context. Contract/source reading has narrowed the discrepancy; a bounded legal schedule is more discriminating than arbitrary malformed messages or additional observer variants.',disposition='concrete_suspicion',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')
sub=dict(action='continue',rationale='Register usable two-core overview and select the sourced read-context consumption discrepancy for responsibility and legal-history investigation.',map_path='map.json',sources=sources,question=q,feedback=dict(ref_ids=['S-read-response','S-read-queue','S-client-batches','S-node-read','S-member-guards'],answered='Follower read completion is exact-context: node batches independently generated SystemCtx values and pendingReadIndex.addReady updates only a matching map key. Thus remote queue-prefix propagation is not explained by a generic latest-context completion rule. Legal RSM membership transitions also prohibit full-member demotion and re-adding removed IDs, constraining the earlier observer eligibility suspicion.',remaining=['Ground the bounded response-correlation responsibility and establish a legal overlapping remote-read history.','Investigate pending read support across permitted membership changes separately.'],understanding='updated',rationale='Map now incorporates actual caller protection, producer restrictions and consumer semantics; no defect attribution or execution is claimed.'))
